<title>CHINA: China sugar output seen up 2.0 mln T in 1996.</title>
<headline>China sugar output seen up 2.0 mln T in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's sugar output could soar by as much as 2.0 million tonnes this year to one of its highest levels on record, the Xinhua news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It quoted Ministry of Agriculture officials at a recent meeting as forecasting the steep upturn in output.</p>
<p>China's sugar output was 5.65 million tonnes in 1995 and state media had forecast output would rise to 6.53 million tonnes in 1996 because of a hike in the state purchasing price.</p>
<p>In the first eight months of 1996, sugar output totalled 4.296 million tonnes, down by 9.17 percent compared with the same period last year, the State Statistical Bureau said on Monday.</p>
